---
import NichePage from '../components/NichePage.astro';
import { policies, khmer } from '../data/business';
import photo from '../assets/photos/team-shirts-tent.jpg';

const faqs = [
  { q: 'When should we book for AAPI Heritage Month?', a: `AAPI Heritage Month is in May. Please book as early as you can, and at least ${policies.leadTimeDays} days ahead.` },
  { q: 'Is Kreung LA AAPI-owned?', a: 'Yes. Kreung LA is owned by Sam Oum and Christina. Sam is Cambodian American, born in Khao-I-Dang, a refugee camp on the Thai-Cambodian border.' },
  { q: 'Can Sam share the story behind the food?', a: 'Tell us what your event needs when you ask for a quote, and we will talk through it with you.' },
  { q: 'How much does it cost?', a: 'Packages are $20, $25 and $33 per person. The minimum is $1,000 for pickup and drop-off and $2,000 for our grill on-site.' },
  { q: 'Can you serve our whole office?', a: `Yes. We cater for ${policies.guestsLabel} guests and deliver to ${policies.deliveryArea}.` },
  { q: 'Do you have vegan options?', a: 'Yes. Our tofu skewers are vegan. Our food contains no dairy or peanuts.' },
];
---
<NichePage
  title="AAPI Heritage Month Catering in Los Angeles | Kreung LA"
  description="Cambodian BBQ catering for AAPI Heritage Month in LA. AAPI-owned, with a family story your team can taste. Book early for May. From $20 per person."
  path="/aapi-heritage-month-catering"
  crumb="AAPI Heritage Month"
  h1="AAPI Heritage Month Catering in Los Angeles"
  lede="Planning a May event for your ERG or the whole office? Celebrate with Cambodian BBQ from an AAPI-owned family business, and a story worth sharing."
  photo={photo}
  photoAlt="The Kreung LA team in matching shirts under their event tent"
  estimateType="Corporate or office lunch"
  estimateNotes="This is for an AAPI Heritage Month event in May."
  reviewKeys={['repeatClient', 'rareBeauty', 'janeT']}
  faqs={faqs}
  faqHeading="AAPI Heritage Month questions"
  ctaHeading="Book early for May."
  ctaText="Get your estimate now and lock in your May date."
  bodyTone="pink"
>
  <div class="cols">
    <div class="prose">
      <h2>A story your team can taste</h2>
      <p>Sam was born in Khao-I-Dang, a refugee camp on the Thai-Cambodian border. His family resettled in North Carolina, far from any Cambodian community.</p>
      <p>For years he told his mother, Mak (<span lang="km">{khmer.mak}</span>), "I'm gonna bring Cambodian food to LA." She passed in late November 2023. Her last words to him were to stop talking and start doing. On January 1, 2024, her birthday, Kreung LA got its first catering order.</p>
      <h2>Culturally specific, not generic</h2>
      <p>Cambodian food is often missing from "Asian" catering menus. Ours is built on kreung, the Khmer herb paste of lemongrass, galangal, turmeric, makrut lime leaves, garlic and shallots. It's a real taste of Cambodia, and a great way to start a conversation.</p>
      <p><a href="/about">Read Sam's story</a> · <a href="/guides/what-is-kreung">What is kreung?</a></p>
    </div>
    <div class="card card--line">
      <h3>Book early for May</h3>
      <p>AAPI Heritage Month is in May. Book as early as you can, and at least {policies.leadTimeDays} days ahead.</p>
      <ul class="check">
        <li>AAPI-owned, family-run</li>
        <li>From $20 per person</li>
        <li>{policies.guestsLabel} guests</li>
        <li>Vegan tofu skewers available</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>
</NichePage>
